        <h2>Our History</h2>
        <p>
            St. Thomas More Catholic Church was established in February 1998 when the
            Archdiocese purchased the former Monavoni Dutch Reformed Church to serve the
            growing Catholic community south of the Old Johannesburg Road in Centurion.
        </p>

        <p>
            The first Mass was celebrated on 8 February 1998 by Archbishop George Daniel.
            Many parishioners came from Maria Regina in Lyttelton, with Fr. Ian Laurenson
            OFM as the first parish priest, followed by Mgr. Vincent Hill in 1999.
        </p>

        <h2>Caritas Ministry</h2>
        <p>
            Caritas is a Christian outreach rooted in the mission of the Catholic Church,
            dedicated to bringing Christ’s light to incarcerated individuals and their families.
        </p>

        <h2>St. Vincent de Paul Solidarity</h2>
        <p>
            The Society of St. Vincent de Paul assists the poor and vulnerable through food
            parcels, clothing, financial support, and companionship.
        </p>

        <h2>Serving the Community</h2>
        <ul class="about-list">
            <li>Celebrating the sacraments and fostering spiritual growth</li>
            <li>Supporting outreach ministries like Caritas and SVP</li>
            <li>Providing youth development and fellowship</li>
            <li>Extending compassion through service and prayer</li>
        </ul>

    </div>

